WEBVTT

00:00:02.769 --> 00:00:05.567
Mr. Tuvok, Mr. Tuvok!

00:00:05.605 --> 00:00:08.665
I was supposed to accompany you
on security rounds this morning.

00:00:08.708 --> 00:00:09.902
Did you forget?

00:00:09.943 --> 00:00:12.104
I was not aware that we had
a definite appointment.

00:00:12.145 --> 00:00:13.737
I'm sure it was definite.

00:00:13.780 --> 00:00:16.305
Well, maybe not
completely definite.

00:00:16.349 --> 00:00:17.976
That is, I'd expressed my desire

00:00:18.084 --> 00:00:19.847
to "learn the ropes,"
as it were,

00:00:19.886 --> 00:00:23.549
and I have completed my study
of starship security protocols.

00:00:23.590 --> 00:00:25.455
I think you'll find
that I'm fully qualified

00:00:25.492 --> 00:00:28.586
to serve in the capacity
of a Starfleet security officer.

00:00:28.628 --> 00:00:30.255
Junior grade, of course.

00:00:30.296 --> 00:00:31.456
If you will recall, Mr. Neelix,

00:00:31.498 --> 00:00:33.625
I did not guarantee you
a position.

00:00:33.666 --> 00:00:35.361
But Captain Janeway
is always saying

00:00:35.402 --> 00:00:37.495
that Voyager is
a ship of opportunity.

00:00:37.537 --> 00:00:40.199
That is true, but opportunities
for promotion

00:00:40.240 --> 00:00:41.969
on a starship must be earned.

00:00:42.008 --> 00:00:44.340
I've been working hard at this.

00:00:44.377 --> 00:00:45.344
I really do feel

00:00:45.378 --> 00:00:48.108
I have a great deal
to contribute to Voyager

00:00:48.148 --> 00:00:49.615
beyond my current role.

00:00:49.649 --> 00:00:52.641
Your dedication
is duly noted, Mr. Neelix.

00:00:52.685 --> 00:00:55.449
Now, if you'll excuse me,
I am due on the Bridge.

00:00:55.488 --> 00:00:57.615
I'll see you first thing
tomorrow morning

00:00:57.657 --> 00:00:58.715
for security rounds.

00:01:04.230 --> 00:01:06.027
Ensign Vorik.

00:01:07.167 --> 00:01:08.759
Get me a duotronic probe.

00:01:08.802 --> 00:01:11.134
I'm having trouble
regulating the plasma flow.

00:01:11.171 --> 00:01:13.571
May I suggest a gravitic
caliper instead?

00:01:13.606 --> 00:01:15.972
You might find it
a more precise instrument.

00:01:16.042 --> 00:01:18.510
Good idea, but bring me both.

00:01:18.545 --> 00:01:20.308
Good morning, B'Elanna.

00:01:20.346 --> 00:01:23.543
You missed my special
Klingon breakfast buffet.

00:01:23.583 --> 00:01:25.847
I'm sorry, Neelix,
but a bowl of cold gagh

00:01:25.885 --> 00:01:27.978
is not my idea
of how to start a morning.

00:01:28.054 --> 00:01:29.351
Well, you're not alone.

00:01:29.389 --> 00:01:30.356
None of the crew seemed

00:01:30.390 --> 00:01:31.914
especially
enthusiastic about it.

00:01:31.958 --> 00:01:36.122
Um, what's the problem with...

00:01:36.162 --> 00:01:37.993
the plasma injectors?

00:01:38.098 --> 00:01:40.794
I've been getting
myself up to speed

00:01:40.834 --> 00:01:42.995
on Federation warp propulsion.

00:01:43.036 --> 00:01:46.472
The plasma flow in the manifold
seems to be constricted.

00:01:46.506 --> 00:01:49.373
Ah! Have you thought
of phase-locking them

00:01:49.409 --> 00:01:51.104
to the dilithium matrix?

00:01:51.144 --> 00:01:52.668
That was the first thing I did.

00:01:52.712 --> 00:01:53.974
Oh.

00:01:56.483 --> 00:01:58.007
I really am interested

00:01:58.084 --> 00:02:00.177
in learning more about
engineering systems,

00:02:00.220 --> 00:02:03.383
maybe even volunteering
for a few duty shifts.

00:02:03.423 --> 00:02:05.220
In fact, I have
a couple of questions

00:02:05.258 --> 00:02:07.123
about the impulse
response filters...

00:02:07.160 --> 00:02:08.718
Neelix, Neelix,

00:02:08.761 --> 00:02:10.752
this really isn't a good time.

00:02:10.797 --> 00:02:12.856
I understand, Lieutenant.

00:02:12.899 --> 00:02:14.628
Sorry.

00:02:16.503 --> 00:02:20.337
I'll just, uh, watch for a while
if you don't mind.

00:02:20.373 --> 00:02:21.840
Here are the tools, sir.

00:02:24.811 --> 00:02:27.541
I also had a question
about the transporter buffers...

00:02:27.580 --> 00:02:30.174
Mr. Neelix,
please report to the Bridge.

00:02:30.216 --> 00:02:32.810
On my way, Captain.

00:02:40.793 --> 00:02:43.318
Neelix, we seem
to be approaching

00:02:43.363 --> 00:02:45.729
some kind of interstellar
dust clouds.

00:02:45.765 --> 00:02:48.427
Can you tell us
anything about them?

00:02:48.468 --> 00:02:50.732
They look rather ominous to me.

00:02:51.838 --> 00:02:55.001
I believe this is
a region of space

00:02:55.108 --> 00:02:57.702
known as the Nekrit Expanse.

00:04:50.555 --> 00:04:54.321
What can you tell us
about this Expanse, Mr. Neelix?

00:04:54.359 --> 00:04:56.452
It's a vast territory.

00:04:56.495 --> 00:04:58.429
No one knows much about it.

00:04:58.463 --> 00:05:01.261
Those plasma storms might be
a problem for navigation.

00:05:01.299 --> 00:05:02.391
Full sensor scan, Tuvok.

00:05:02.434 --> 00:05:03.423
Aye, Captain.

00:05:03.468 --> 00:05:05.129
Can we plot a course around it?

00:05:05.170 --> 00:05:07.263
That might be advisable.

00:05:07.305 --> 00:05:08.499
I don't believe so.

00:05:08.540 --> 00:05:10.531
It's thousands
of light-years wide.

00:05:10.575 --> 00:05:12.668
Then we'll have
to go through it.

00:05:12.711 --> 00:05:13.871
Looks like we'll be counting

00:05:13.912 --> 00:05:15.243
on your knowledge
of the Delta Quadrant

00:05:15.280 --> 00:05:17.271
even more than usual, Neelix.

00:05:18.850 --> 00:05:20.374
Yes, ma'am.

00:05:20.419 --> 00:05:22.649
I'm at your command, as always.

00:05:22.687 --> 00:05:25.485
Will there be any planets
where we can take on supplies?

00:05:25.524 --> 00:05:28.084
There is a station
near the border...

00:05:28.126 --> 00:05:31.186
a kind of supply depot
for mining and trading ships.

00:05:31.229 --> 00:05:33.163
I suggest we stop there
for provisions

00:05:33.198 --> 00:05:35.132
before we go
into the Nekrit Expanse.

00:05:35.167 --> 00:05:37.260
What are the coordinates?

00:05:37.302 --> 00:05:39.327
Uh, let's see.

00:05:39.371 --> 00:05:41.236
It's actually been a while...

00:05:41.273 --> 00:05:43.332
I have the station on sensors,
Captain.

00:05:43.375 --> 00:05:45.343
3.4 light-years away,

00:05:45.377 --> 00:05:47.675
heading 071 mark 17.

00:05:47.712 --> 00:05:48.679
You heard him, Tom.

00:05:48.713 --> 00:05:50.146
On our way.

00:05:55.987 --> 00:05:57.648
We're being hailed, Captain.

00:05:57.689 --> 00:05:58.815
On screen.

00:06:01.093 --> 00:06:02.890
I'm Captain Kathryn Janeway

00:06:02.928 --> 00:06:05.396
of the Federation
Starship Voyager.

00:06:05.430 --> 00:06:07.898
Bahrat, manager of this station.

00:06:07.933 --> 00:06:09.025
What can I do for you?

00:06:09.067 --> 00:06:12.332
Your station is
a trading outpost, isn't it?

00:06:12.370 --> 00:06:14.099
I'd like permission
to come aboard

00:06:14.139 --> 00:06:15.538
to negotiate for supplies.

00:06:15.574 --> 00:06:17.599
Granted,

00:06:17.642 --> 00:06:19.940
but understand
that any transaction

00:06:20.011 --> 00:06:23.174
you negotiate on this station
is subject to my approval.

00:06:23.215 --> 00:06:26.116
I receive a 20 percent
commission on all trade.

00:06:26.151 --> 00:06:29.177
Your whereabouts
will be closely monitored.

00:06:29.221 --> 00:06:30.552
Communications with your ship

00:06:30.589 --> 00:06:34.081
may also be monitored
at my discretion.

00:06:34.126 --> 00:06:35.684
Do you agree
to these conditions?

00:06:35.727 --> 00:06:37.854
Evidently, I have no choice.

00:06:37.896 --> 00:06:39.158
Excellent.

00:06:39.197 --> 00:06:40.960
Meet me in my office in one hour

00:06:40.999 --> 00:06:43.335
and we'll discuss your needs.

00:06:43.468 --> 00:06:45.902
Pleasant fellow.

00:06:45.937 --> 00:06:48.337
Neelix, Chakotay, Tom...
you're with me.

00:07:09.060 --> 00:07:10.425
Mr. Bahrat.

00:07:10.462 --> 00:07:11.724
What is it?

00:07:13.531 --> 00:07:14.998
I'm Kathryn Janeway.

00:07:16.901 --> 00:07:19.597
I've brought a list
of the supplies we'll need.

00:07:19.637 --> 00:07:21.935
Forgive me,
but it's demanding work

00:07:22.040 --> 00:07:23.940
watching over this station.

00:07:23.975 --> 00:07:26.944
We get all kinds
of troublemakers here.

00:07:27.045 --> 00:07:28.205
I understand.

00:07:29.514 --> 00:07:31.311
All right. Let's see it.

00:07:34.919 --> 00:07:36.716
Hmm.

00:07:36.755 --> 00:07:39.121
Mm-hmm.

00:07:39.157 --> 00:07:41.751
Hmm... pergium?

00:07:41.793 --> 00:07:42.782
To regenerate the filters

00:07:42.827 --> 00:07:45.091
in our environmental
control system.

00:07:45.130 --> 00:07:47.530
That might be
a little difficult.

00:07:47.565 --> 00:07:49.396
It's a rare commodity.

00:07:49.434 --> 00:07:50.492
Give me a few moments

00:07:50.535 --> 00:07:53.129
and I'll put together a list
of potential suppliers,

00:07:53.171 --> 00:07:56.800
but I'll warn you...
they won't strike

00:07:56.841 --> 00:07:58.172
easy bargains.

00:07:58.209 --> 00:08:00.200
I'm prepared to deal fairly.

00:08:28.306 --> 00:08:31.332
Good day, gentlemen.
Good day.

00:08:31.376 --> 00:08:33.503
Anything in particular
you're looking for?

00:08:33.545 --> 00:08:34.944
Anything I can help you with?

00:08:35.046 --> 00:08:37.037
We were hoping to find
some magnetic spindle bearings

00:08:37.081 --> 00:08:39.276
for our reaction
control assembly.

00:08:39.317 --> 00:08:42.184
Spindle bearings,
spindle bearings...

00:08:42.220 --> 00:08:44.950
No. Can't help you
with that. No.

00:08:44.989 --> 00:08:46.513
Long voyage ahead?

00:08:46.558 --> 00:08:48.788
Uh, you could say that.

00:08:49.994 --> 00:08:52.326
I have something
that might ease your journey,

00:08:52.363 --> 00:08:53.955
ease it considerably.

00:08:54.032 --> 00:08:56.091
Rhuludian crystals.

00:08:56.134 --> 00:08:59.228
Ingesting just one of these
will make days of tedious travel

00:08:59.270 --> 00:09:01.170
seem like moments
of exquisite rapture.

00:09:01.206 --> 00:09:03.470
No, thank you.

00:09:03.508 --> 00:09:05.032
The price is surprisingly...

00:09:05.076 --> 00:09:06.134
No.

00:09:08.279 --> 00:09:09.974
Nice place.

00:09:18.490 --> 00:09:20.048
I see you're a map dealer.

00:09:20.091 --> 00:09:21.353
I have coordinate charts

00:09:21.392 --> 00:09:23.326
for all of the local
mining colonies.

00:09:23.361 --> 00:09:27.457
Actually, I'm interested
in maps of the Nekrit Expanse.

00:09:27.499 --> 00:09:29.558
You must be a stranger here
or you'd know.

00:09:29.601 --> 00:09:31.330
There aren't any maps
of that region.

00:09:31.369 --> 00:09:34.304
Surely, there's an astrometric
chart or a database

00:09:34.339 --> 00:09:36.170
that would help me plot
a safe course.

00:09:36.207 --> 00:09:39.301
The Nekrit Expanse is
too unstable to chart.

00:09:39.344 --> 00:09:40.641
No matter.

00:09:40.678 --> 00:09:43.476
He never could plot
a straight course anyway.

00:09:43.515 --> 00:09:45.380
Wixiban?

00:09:45.416 --> 00:09:49.284
Wix, is that you?

00:09:51.089 --> 00:09:53.216
I can't believe it.

00:09:53.258 --> 00:09:56.523
What are you doing here?

00:09:56.561 --> 00:09:59.826
I've never seen another Talaxian
this far from home.

00:09:59.864 --> 00:10:00.922
It's a long story.

00:10:00.965 --> 00:10:03.525
I'm one of the crew
of a highly-advanced starship.

00:10:03.568 --> 00:10:07.470
Ah... I want
to hear all about it.

00:10:07.505 --> 00:10:08.904
Come on.

00:10:08.940 --> 00:10:10.737
The tavern here serves
the best Toffa ale

00:10:10.775 --> 00:10:12.743
I've had in years.

00:10:12.777 --> 00:10:14.972
I do a little of everything...

00:10:15.013 --> 00:10:16.275
cook, guide,

00:10:16.314 --> 00:10:18.179
advisor to the Captain.

00:10:18.216 --> 00:10:21.447
Possibly even
an unofficial ambassador.

00:10:21.486 --> 00:10:24.751
Life's been good to you.

00:10:24.789 --> 00:10:29.021
Yes, I'm very... I'm very lucky.

00:10:32.130 --> 00:10:34.530
Mmm... but what about you?

00:10:34.566 --> 00:10:36.329
What are you doing
on this station?

00:10:36.367 --> 00:10:39.803
A little of this,
a little of that.

00:10:39.837 --> 00:10:41.862
To tell you the truth,

00:10:41.906 --> 00:10:45.740
things haven't gone
quite so well for me.

00:10:46.878 --> 00:10:48.209
I'm sorry.

00:10:48.246 --> 00:10:52.012
Ever since that nasty business
with the Ubeans,

00:10:52.083 --> 00:10:53.983
things have been difficult.

00:10:54.018 --> 00:10:55.815
But you know me.

00:10:55.853 --> 00:10:58.413
Can't keep Wix down long.

00:10:58.456 --> 00:11:00.720
I'm working on a trade deal now

00:11:00.758 --> 00:11:05.092
that should put me right back
in the thick of things again.

00:11:05.129 --> 00:11:06.790
I hope it works out.

00:11:06.831 --> 00:11:08.560
Yeah.

00:11:08.600 --> 00:11:10.795
Uh, Wix...

00:11:10.835 --> 00:11:13.235
about the Ubeans.

00:11:13.271 --> 00:11:18.299
I don't think I ever told you
how much I valued what you did.

00:11:18.343 --> 00:11:20.937
You'd have done the same for me.

00:11:20.979 --> 00:11:23.971
Yes, I would have, but you
were the one who got caught.

00:11:24.015 --> 00:11:27.451
I owe you a great deal.

00:11:27.485 --> 00:11:28.975
If there's anything
I can do to help...

00:11:29.020 --> 00:11:30.146
I'm fine.

00:11:30.188 --> 00:11:32.088
Honestly.

00:11:32.123 --> 00:11:35.957
Maybe not on the crew
of a magnificent starship,

00:11:35.994 --> 00:11:37.461
but I'll get by.

00:11:37.495 --> 00:11:40.157
To tell you the truth, um...

00:11:40.198 --> 00:11:41.597
it's not quite what I told you.

00:11:41.633 --> 00:11:44.932
In fact, I may not be on Voyager
much longer.

00:11:44.969 --> 00:11:46.834
Why?

00:11:46.871 --> 00:11:51.467
The main reason Captain Janeway
needed me was as a guide

00:11:51.509 --> 00:11:54.000
to give her information
about this Quadrant,

00:11:54.045 --> 00:11:56.513
but I've never been
beyond the Nekrit Expanse.

00:11:56.547 --> 00:11:58.981
I can't tell her anything
about what's ahead.

00:11:59.017 --> 00:12:01.281
But your other jobs...

00:12:01.319 --> 00:12:03.947
cook, ambassador?

00:12:04.055 --> 00:12:06.922
They don't really need a cook

00:12:06.958 --> 00:12:12.294
and I don't think our Captain
really requires an ambassador.

00:12:12.330 --> 00:12:14.958
I've tried to find
some other area

00:12:14.999 --> 00:12:17.490
where I might be useful, but...

00:12:17.535 --> 00:12:20.698
the truth is...

00:12:20.738 --> 00:12:23.332
I'm not needed.

00:12:25.910 --> 00:12:27.502
I'm hoping you can help me.

00:12:27.545 --> 00:12:29.513
I can't let Voyager go

00:12:29.547 --> 00:12:31.447
into that dangerous part
of space

00:12:31.482 --> 00:12:33.450
without some idea
of what's there.

00:12:33.484 --> 00:12:35.384
I have to find a map.

00:12:37.021 --> 00:12:38.716
Hmm.

00:12:48.533 --> 00:12:51.400
Can I be of help, Mr. Neelix?

00:12:51.436 --> 00:12:53.461
Dinner isn't for another hour,
Ensign Vorik,

00:12:53.504 --> 00:12:55.438
and I don't have time
to prepare a snack.

00:12:55.473 --> 00:12:57.441
I don't require food
at the moment.

00:12:57.475 --> 00:12:59.102
Lieutenant Torres
sent me to adjust

00:12:59.143 --> 00:13:01.373
the control interface
in your food replicators.

00:13:01.412 --> 00:13:03.676
You said you were experiencing
difficulties with them.

00:13:03.715 --> 00:13:05.774
Oh, of course.

00:13:05.817 --> 00:13:07.148
Go ahead.

00:13:10.121 --> 00:13:11.247
Neelix...

00:13:11.289 --> 00:13:12.620
I thought you'd like
to say hello

00:13:12.657 --> 00:13:13.646
to your old friend.

00:13:15.326 --> 00:13:17.123
Well, uh...

00:13:17.161 --> 00:13:19.959
yes, yes, of course.

00:13:19.997 --> 00:13:24.661
So, this is where you prepare
your legendary feasts.

00:13:24.702 --> 00:13:25.760
Well...

00:13:25.803 --> 00:13:28.829
You know, Commander,
Neelix has more varied talents

00:13:28.873 --> 00:13:30.932
than anyone I've ever known.

00:13:30.975 --> 00:13:33.102
You're lucky to have him
on board.

00:13:33.144 --> 00:13:35.806
Mr. Wix was able to find
those magnetic spindle bearings

00:13:35.847 --> 00:13:36.814
we were looking for.

00:13:36.848 --> 00:13:37.974
I don't know
what we'd have done

00:13:38.082 --> 00:13:39.208
if he hadn't come up with them.

00:13:39.250 --> 00:13:42.481
Well, yes, Wix has
always had a knack

00:13:42.520 --> 00:13:45.522
for finding
those hard-to-locate items.

00:13:46.990 --> 00:13:49.618
I'll let you two
reminisce for a while.

00:13:49.659 --> 00:13:50.956
Thanks again, Wix.

00:13:50.994 --> 00:13:52.484
You're more than welcome.

00:13:52.529 --> 00:13:53.860
Yes, this is the mess room.

00:13:53.897 --> 00:13:55.660
On any given day,
I must be prepared

00:13:55.698 --> 00:13:57.290
to feed over a hundred people.

00:13:57.333 --> 00:13:59.494
About done, Ensign?

00:13:59.536 --> 00:14:01.629
Not quite.

00:14:01.671 --> 00:14:04.196
Well, I really don't need
the replicators today,

00:14:04.240 --> 00:14:05.730
so, you can finish later.

00:14:05.775 --> 00:14:07.572
As you wish.

00:14:07.610 --> 00:14:08.872
Oh, and remind
Lieutenant Torres,

00:14:08.912 --> 00:14:11.176
uh, when she has a moment,

00:14:11.214 --> 00:14:13.341
I'd still like to go over
a few things with her.

00:14:13.383 --> 00:14:14.907
I'll relay the message.

00:14:14.951 --> 00:14:16.748
Thank you.

00:14:18.154 --> 00:14:19.382
Wix...

00:14:21.658 --> 00:14:23.319
please tell me
those spindle bearings

00:14:23.359 --> 00:14:24.826
weren't stolen property.

00:14:24.861 --> 00:14:27.091
Of course not.

00:14:27.130 --> 00:14:28.893
I wouldn't do that to you.

00:14:30.733 --> 00:14:32.530
Neelix, I need the work.

00:14:32.569 --> 00:14:34.867
I don't live
on a comfortable starship.

00:14:34.904 --> 00:14:37.498
No one looks out for me
except me.

00:14:37.540 --> 00:14:39.838
Maybe you've forgotten
what that feels like.

00:14:39.876 --> 00:14:41.366
I haven't forgotten.

00:14:41.411 --> 00:14:42.878
I've been stuck

00:14:42.912 --> 00:14:45.437
on that trash-heap of a space
station for three years.

00:14:45.481 --> 00:14:46.948
My ship's been impounded.

00:14:46.983 --> 00:14:49.884
I can't afford to give Bahrat
what he wants to get it back.

00:14:49.919 --> 00:14:52.513
Do you begrudge me
an opportunity

00:14:52.555 --> 00:14:54.386
to make a fair trade?

00:14:54.424 --> 00:14:56.984
Of course not.

00:14:57.060 --> 00:14:58.493
I have news for you.

00:14:58.528 --> 00:15:00.553
I've located some pergium
for your ship.

00:15:00.597 --> 00:15:02.292
That's great news.

00:15:02.332 --> 00:15:04.926
Captain Janeway
hasn't had any luck.

00:15:05.001 --> 00:15:06.935
And I've found someone
with a map.

00:15:07.003 --> 00:15:08.834
Wonderful!

00:15:08.871 --> 00:15:10.805
How do we get it?

00:15:10.840 --> 00:15:13.138
Lt'll involve several
bartering sessions.

00:15:13.176 --> 00:15:14.905
I have the opportunity

00:15:14.944 --> 00:15:16.935
to sell medical supplies
to an outpost

00:15:17.013 --> 00:15:19.641
whose people are dying
of a lung disease.

00:15:19.682 --> 00:15:21.877
It's a good cause
and it will make me enough

00:15:21.918 --> 00:15:23.579
to pay Bahrat
and get my ship back.

00:15:23.620 --> 00:15:25.053
Where does the map come in?

00:15:25.088 --> 00:15:27.556
When I deliver
the medical supplies,

00:15:27.590 --> 00:15:31.082
one of the physicians will
give me an astrometric chart.

00:15:31.127 --> 00:15:34.221
I can't thank you enough.

00:15:36.165 --> 00:15:38.395
I'll have to ask your help
though.

00:15:38.434 --> 00:15:39.833
We'll need a shuttle.

00:15:39.869 --> 00:15:41.632
First, we have to get
to a nearby freighter

00:15:41.671 --> 00:15:42.968
to pick up the medical supplies.

00:15:43.039 --> 00:15:45.667
Then, we return
to the space station

00:15:45.708 --> 00:15:48.302
and meet with one of the
physicians from the outpost.

00:15:48.344 --> 00:15:49.971
With your transporter
technology,

00:15:50.046 --> 00:15:52.742
we could be in and out
of the station within minutes.

00:15:52.782 --> 00:15:55.307
Then, I could finally
get away from here

00:15:55.351 --> 00:15:57.478
and get back
to a Talaxian colony.

00:15:57.520 --> 00:15:59.647
I don't think that
would be a problem.

00:15:59.689 --> 00:16:02.522
Just one thing.

00:16:02.558 --> 00:16:04.526
Don't tell anyone
that we're delivering

00:16:04.560 --> 00:16:05.925
medical supplies
to the station...

00:16:06.029 --> 00:16:08.020
not even one person.

00:16:08.064 --> 00:16:09.053
If Bahrat finds out,

00:16:09.098 --> 00:16:11.157
he'll take 20 percent
and I can't afford that.

00:16:11.200 --> 00:16:14.931
I-I suppose there's
no need to mention it.

00:16:14.971 --> 00:16:16.836
Thanks, Neelix.

00:16:16.873 --> 00:16:19.000
I knew I could count on you.

00:16:30.520 --> 00:16:32.784
Didn't I tell you
this would be easy?

00:16:34.290 --> 00:16:36.315
I got the medical supplies

00:16:36.359 --> 00:16:38.953
and you got the pergium
your ship needs so badly.

00:16:38.995 --> 00:16:39.962
Only 20 kilograms.

00:16:39.996 --> 00:16:42.965
I told Commander Chakotay
it would be 45.

00:16:43.032 --> 00:16:45.057
You're lucky to get
what you did.

00:16:45.101 --> 00:16:46.966
Come on, Neelix.

00:16:47.070 --> 00:16:49.265
A few minutes more
and we'll be done.

00:16:49.305 --> 00:16:53.833
And you'll have a map to help
you through the Nekrit Expanse.

00:16:53.876 --> 00:16:56.344
What is the matter with you?

00:16:56.379 --> 00:16:59.075
I don't like keeping the whole
truth from Commander Chakotay.

00:16:59.115 --> 00:17:00.241
It's not honest.

00:17:00.283 --> 00:17:01.648
I don't remember you

00:17:01.684 --> 00:17:05.085
ever being so squeamish
about twisting the truth.

00:17:05.121 --> 00:17:07.419
Wix...

00:17:07.457 --> 00:17:09.721
I'm not what I used to be.

00:17:11.427 --> 00:17:13.918
Neither am I.

00:17:13.963 --> 00:17:16.193
We've both tried
to change our lives.

00:17:16.232 --> 00:17:17.927
You've done it.

00:17:18.034 --> 00:17:20.434
Now, I have the same chance.

00:17:22.505 --> 00:17:23.938
We're almost there.

00:17:23.973 --> 00:17:27.272
We should have your transporter
take us to Corridor 14-L

00:17:27.310 --> 00:17:28.937
near the outer docking ports.

00:17:29.045 --> 00:17:30.512
It's hardly ever used.

00:17:30.546 --> 00:17:32.275
Our contact will meet us there.

00:17:32.315 --> 00:17:34.715
We're within transporter range.

00:17:34.751 --> 00:17:36.878
I've entered the coordinates.

00:17:43.693 --> 00:17:44.819
What are you doing?!

00:17:44.861 --> 00:17:47.955
This station
is a dangerous place

00:17:48.064 --> 00:17:49.759
and these supplies
are valuable.

00:17:49.799 --> 00:17:51.926
We have to be able
to defend ourselves.

00:17:51.968 --> 00:17:54.129
You said this would be easy.

00:17:54.170 --> 00:17:56.001
It's just a precaution.

00:17:59.842 --> 00:18:01.537
Let's go.

00:18:01.577 --> 00:18:03.340
Computer, energize.

00:18:16.626 --> 00:18:18.184
Where's your contact?

00:18:18.227 --> 00:18:19.251
He'll be here.

00:18:19.295 --> 00:18:21.525
Don't worry.

00:18:21.564 --> 00:18:22.531
I don't like this...

00:18:22.565 --> 00:18:25.090
meeting in dark passageways
late at night.

00:18:25.134 --> 00:18:26.123
Wix.

00:18:27.470 --> 00:18:29.370
Sutok.

00:18:31.607 --> 00:18:33.666
This is my associate.

00:18:34.877 --> 00:18:36.310
You have the supplies?

00:18:36.345 --> 00:18:38.370
As promised.

00:18:51.694 --> 00:18:52.922
What's he doing?

00:18:54.330 --> 00:18:55.854
Satisfied?

00:18:56.999 --> 00:18:58.967
Completely.

00:18:59.068 --> 00:19:01.662
What kind of medical
supplies are those?

00:19:01.704 --> 00:19:05.765
If you give me my payment,
we'll be on our way.

00:19:05.808 --> 00:19:08.834
Yes, I have it right here.

00:19:16.819 --> 00:19:18.150
Stop them!
Get his weapon!

00:19:18.187 --> 00:19:19.154
Wix!

00:19:19.188 --> 00:19:20.815
Someone's coming!

00:19:23.192 --> 00:19:25.353
Neelix!

00:19:26.362 --> 00:19:28.694
Get us out of here.

00:19:28.731 --> 00:19:31.529
Computer, two to beam up.

00:19:38.474 --> 00:19:40.499
You lied to me
from the beginning!

00:19:40.543 --> 00:19:42.306
And I was foolish enough
to believe you.

00:19:42.345 --> 00:19:44.609
It should have been
as easy as I said.

00:19:44.647 --> 00:19:47.810
I didn't know Sutok
would try to steal the tubes.

00:19:47.850 --> 00:19:50.114
Those aren't ordinary
medical supplies.

00:19:50.152 --> 00:19:51.949
You failed to mention that.

00:19:52.054 --> 00:19:54.215
They do have
a medicinal application,

00:19:54.257 --> 00:19:56.691
but no one would pay
what I was supposed to get

00:19:56.726 --> 00:19:58.591
if they were just
simple medications.

00:19:58.628 --> 00:20:01.119
They're narcotics, aren't they?

00:20:02.899 --> 00:20:05.629
Oh, you're up
to your same old tricks.

00:20:07.570 --> 00:20:09.470
We have to talk
to Captain Janeway

00:20:09.505 --> 00:20:10.870
as soon as we get back.

00:20:13.776 --> 00:20:16.244
Do you really want to do that?

00:20:16.279 --> 00:20:18.406
How is it going to look
to your shipmates

00:20:18.447 --> 00:20:21.712
when they find out you were
once a contraband smuggler

00:20:21.751 --> 00:20:24.879
and that you were involved
in this ugly business tonight?

00:20:24.921 --> 00:20:29.756
You think your position
on Voyager is precarious now?

00:20:29.792 --> 00:20:33.387
Wait till they discover
the whole truth about you.

00:20:33.429 --> 00:20:35.659
I can't just forget about this.

00:20:35.698 --> 00:20:40.101
So you'd let Bahrat put me
in cryostatic suspension?

00:20:43.439 --> 00:20:45.839
I guess you would.

00:20:45.875 --> 00:20:49.003
You did let me spend a year
in that Ubean prison.

00:20:49.045 --> 00:20:50.745
Wix...

00:20:50.878 --> 00:20:52.812
I never told you what it
was like in there, did I?

00:20:52.847 --> 00:20:55.213
About eating worms
to stay alive...

00:20:55.249 --> 00:20:56.682
sleeping in a cell

00:20:56.717 --> 00:20:59.618
where the vermin
chew on you all night...

00:20:59.653 --> 00:21:02.053
being punished in ways
you couldn't imagine.

00:21:02.089 --> 00:21:03.522
All right!

00:21:07.027 --> 00:21:09.188
I won't say anything.

00:21:10.898 --> 00:21:14.265
But I don't want to have
anything more to do with you.

00:21:14.301 --> 00:21:16.565
The debt is paid.

00:21:20.608 --> 00:21:22.974
Captain's Log, supplemental.

00:21:23.043 --> 00:21:24.772
I have called a meeting
of the senior staff

00:21:24.812 --> 00:21:27.178
to inform them
of some very disturbing news

00:21:27.214 --> 00:21:29.580
I have just received.

00:21:34.722 --> 00:21:36.815
There's been a murder
aboard the station.

00:21:36.857 --> 00:21:37.983
A murder?

00:21:38.025 --> 00:21:41.188
I've been told that's not
an uncommon occurrence here.

00:21:41.228 --> 00:21:44.629
The man who died has been
suspected of criminal activity.

00:21:44.665 --> 00:21:47.657
Mr. Bahrat, however, discovered
something at the scene

00:21:47.701 --> 00:21:50.226
of the killing
that greatly concerns me.

00:21:50.271 --> 00:21:51.602
During my investigation,

00:21:51.639 --> 00:21:54.403
I discovered some energy
readings I couldn't identify,

00:21:54.441 --> 00:21:57.672
so I ran a spectral analysis.

00:21:57.711 --> 00:22:00.544
He showed me the analysis
just a few minutes ago.

00:22:00.581 --> 00:22:04.312
It's a Federation
phaser signature.

00:22:04.351 --> 00:22:08.185
Tuvok will be assisting Mr.
Bahrat in his investigation.

00:22:08.222 --> 00:22:10.782
I want to know how a weapon
from Voyager

00:22:10.825 --> 00:22:12.952
could have been involved
in this incident.

00:22:13.060 --> 00:22:14.186
The shooting took place

00:22:14.228 --> 00:22:16.128
in an abandoned section
of the station.

00:22:16.163 --> 00:22:18.631
Security scanners were disabled.

00:22:18.666 --> 00:22:21.965
I'm reviewing
other surveillance records,

00:22:22.002 --> 00:22:24.937
looking for anything
that might help me apprehend

00:22:24.972 --> 00:22:27.099
whoever did this.

00:22:27.141 --> 00:22:28.938
I've promised Mr. Bahrat
the full cooperation

00:22:28.976 --> 00:22:32.468
of every member of this crew
during his investigation.

00:22:32.513 --> 00:22:34.708
Dismissed.

00:22:56.704 --> 00:22:58.865
You wanted to see me, Mr. Tuvok?

00:22:58.906 --> 00:23:00.703
Please, sit down.

00:23:00.741 --> 00:23:03.505
I examined the scene
of the shooting

00:23:03.544 --> 00:23:05.637
and confirmed the Federation
weapon signature...

00:23:05.679 --> 00:23:07.146
a type-2 phaser blast.

00:23:07.181 --> 00:23:09.308
14 Voyager crew members
were off the ship

00:23:09.350 --> 00:23:10.908
at the time of the incident.

00:23:10.951 --> 00:23:12.418
I see.

00:23:12.453 --> 00:23:14.853
Several traders from the station

00:23:14.889 --> 00:23:17.357
were aboard Voyager
on the day of the incident.

00:23:17.391 --> 00:23:19.052
We can't rule out
the possibility

00:23:19.093 --> 00:23:21.357
that one of them managed
to steal a phaser.

00:23:21.395 --> 00:23:23.260
I suppose not.

00:23:23.297 --> 00:23:25.857
What can you tell me
about your friend Wixiban?

00:23:25.900 --> 00:23:27.231
Wix?

00:23:27.268 --> 00:23:29.828
Mr. Chakotay reported
that he was aboard Voyager.

00:23:32.172 --> 00:23:36.609
Ah, yes. He delivered
some magnetic bearings.

00:23:39.046 --> 00:23:41.514
We're more like acquaintances,
not friends really.

00:23:41.548 --> 00:23:42.947
I haven't seen him in years.

00:23:42.983 --> 00:23:45.110
Has he ever been involved
in criminal activity?

00:23:45.152 --> 00:23:47.518
I-I wouldn't know.

00:23:47.554 --> 00:23:49.385
I certainly don't think so.

00:23:50.424 --> 00:23:52.722
I must question him

00:23:52.760 --> 00:23:54.921
and I would appreciate
your accompanying me.

00:23:54.962 --> 00:23:56.657
Me?

00:23:56.697 --> 00:23:58.187
What could I do?

00:23:58.232 --> 00:23:59.824
You may be able to help me
evaluate

00:23:59.867 --> 00:24:01.528
the verisimilitude
of his answers.

00:24:01.568 --> 00:24:02.535
I see.

00:24:02.569 --> 00:24:03.763
Please meet me

00:24:03.804 --> 00:24:06.295
in Transporter Room 2
at 1800 hours.

00:24:22.523 --> 00:24:26.152
How much time did you spend
aboard Voyager?

00:24:26.193 --> 00:24:29.162
Probably less than an hour
altogether.

00:24:29.196 --> 00:24:31.562
Were you ever alone on the ship?

00:24:31.598 --> 00:24:36.968
No. I was met by Mr. Chakotay
in your transporter room...

00:24:37.037 --> 00:24:41.940
extraordinary experience
that transporter of yours.

00:24:41.976 --> 00:24:44.672
We delivered the bearings
to Lieutenant Torres.

00:24:44.712 --> 00:24:46.907
Then, Mr. Chakotay and I
paid a visit

00:24:46.947 --> 00:24:49.973
to my old friend Neelix
in your Mess Hall.

00:24:50.017 --> 00:24:52.076
Where were you
at the time of the shooting?

00:24:52.119 --> 00:24:55.145
In bed, asleep.

00:24:55.189 --> 00:24:56.850
Can anyone corroborate that?

00:24:56.890 --> 00:25:01.793
Alas, Mr. Tuvok, I sleep alone.

00:25:01.829 --> 00:25:04.764
That will be all for now,
Mr. Wix.

00:25:06.834 --> 00:25:09.667
I'd like to stay
for a glass of Toffa ale.

00:25:09.703 --> 00:25:11.170
As you wish, but please see me

00:25:11.205 --> 00:25:12.934
as soon as you return
to the ship.

00:25:12.973 --> 00:25:13.962
Yeah.

00:25:21.382 --> 00:25:25.580
I'd forgotten how easy it is
for you to lie.

00:25:25.619 --> 00:25:28.452
You're not suggesting
I tell him the truth.

00:25:28.489 --> 00:25:32.391
Vulcans aren't as easily fooled
as you might think.

00:25:32.426 --> 00:25:34.951
If you want to worry,
I'll give you something

00:25:35.062 --> 00:25:36.893
to worry about.

00:25:36.930 --> 00:25:38.659
What?

00:25:38.699 --> 00:25:43.796
The people I was conducting
that transaction for

00:25:43.837 --> 00:25:46.465
aren't happy that they
didn't get paid.

00:25:46.507 --> 00:25:48.839
I thought this was your scheme.

00:25:48.876 --> 00:25:52.403
Do you think I could have
afforded those tubes?

00:25:52.446 --> 00:25:57.713
I was acting as an agent
for some Kolaati Traders.

00:25:57.751 --> 00:25:59.719
Do you know anything
about the Kolaati?

00:25:59.753 --> 00:26:02.153
They're mean as fire snakes.

00:26:02.189 --> 00:26:04.919
They will kill us,
and it won't be quick.

00:26:05.025 --> 00:26:09.724
I... I can't believe
this is happening.

00:26:09.763 --> 00:26:12.061
Why did I ever listen to you?!

00:26:12.099 --> 00:26:14.932
Neelix, it's all right.

00:26:14.968 --> 00:26:17.869
I've convinced them to take
something else in payment...

00:26:17.905 --> 00:26:20.601
something easily come by.

00:26:20.641 --> 00:26:22.666
They know about Voyager.

00:26:22.709 --> 00:26:26.406
They want a sample
of your ship's warp plasma.

00:26:26.447 --> 00:26:28.039
They'll be able to use it

00:26:28.082 --> 00:26:30.846
to increase the efficiency
of their engines.

00:26:30.884 --> 00:26:33.785
No. It's wrong.
I won't do it.

00:26:33.821 --> 00:26:35.049
This has to stop.

00:26:35.089 --> 00:26:37.455
You should have thought
of that in the beginning.

00:26:37.491 --> 00:26:38.958
You're in too deeply now.

00:26:38.992 --> 00:26:42.291
The people on Voyager
are my friends.

00:26:42.329 --> 00:26:44.422
I can't steal from them.

00:26:44.465 --> 00:26:46.456
Friends?

00:26:46.500 --> 00:26:47.933
You've already told me

00:26:47.968 --> 00:26:50.436
they're ready to put
you off the ship.

00:26:54.441 --> 00:26:56.875
You're living in a dream world.

00:26:56.910 --> 00:26:59.140
It's time to wake up.

00:27:01.281 --> 00:27:04.045
You're on your own,
just as I am

00:27:04.084 --> 00:27:06.109
and you're going to die
a horrible death

00:27:06.153 --> 00:27:07.552
at the hands of the Kolaati

00:27:07.588 --> 00:27:11.217
unless you bring them
three grams of warp plasma.

00:27:11.258 --> 00:27:12.919
Do you understand that?

00:27:13.026 --> 00:27:15.859
I've already told them
you'd do it.

00:27:15.896 --> 00:27:22.028
Meet me here tomorrow morning
at 900 hours.

00:27:36.850 --> 00:27:39.751
Hey, Neelix, what's up?

00:27:39.786 --> 00:27:41.413
Oh, nothing.

00:27:41.455 --> 00:27:45.448
Just thought I might
give you a hand with...

00:27:45.492 --> 00:27:47.926
whatever it is you're doing.

00:27:47.961 --> 00:27:49.952
You may regret that.

00:27:49.997 --> 00:27:51.692
Chakotay and I have to pick up

00:27:51.732 --> 00:27:54.257
a supply of biomimetic gel
tomorrow morning

00:27:54.301 --> 00:27:56.769
and I am trying
to find the container

00:27:56.803 --> 00:27:59.036
that is listed as the proper
transport device.

00:27:59.169 --> 00:28:03.401
Starfleet standard issue L647 X7.

00:28:03.440 --> 00:28:06.671
Well, sounds like another
set of eyes wouldn't hurt.

00:28:08.378 --> 00:28:09.811
M-34...

00:28:09.846 --> 00:28:10.972
No, not that one.

00:28:14.017 --> 00:28:16.349
L647...

00:28:16.386 --> 00:28:18.115
No, it's Y-6.

00:28:22.826 --> 00:28:24.225
Tom...

00:28:28.065 --> 00:28:29.589
if it's not too bold of me,

00:28:29.633 --> 00:28:31.567
I wonder if I could
ask you something.

00:28:31.601 --> 00:28:33.398
Sure. Anything.

00:28:33.437 --> 00:28:36.565
I've heard you were
in some trouble in the past.

00:28:36.606 --> 00:28:38.699
Spent time in prison.

00:28:38.742 --> 00:28:40.733
That's right.

00:28:40.777 --> 00:28:42.711
Do you?

00:28:44.081 --> 00:28:47.676
Would you... tell me
how you got in trouble?

00:28:50.587 --> 00:28:52.919
I've thought a lot
about that

00:28:52.956 --> 00:28:55.925
and it comes down
to one simple fact.

00:28:55.959 --> 00:28:57.893
I didn't tell the truth.

00:28:57.928 --> 00:29:01.557
I made a mistake,
which happens to people,

00:29:01.598 --> 00:29:03.532
but if I'd admitted
that mistake,

00:29:03.567 --> 00:29:05.501
it would have been a lot better.

00:29:07.037 --> 00:29:09.130
But I lied about it

00:29:09.172 --> 00:29:11.663
and it nearly ruined my life.

00:29:12.776 --> 00:29:15.006
Why do you ask?

00:29:15.045 --> 00:29:18.276
Oh... no reason.

00:29:21.384 --> 00:29:23.147
Just wondered.

00:29:29.493 --> 00:29:31.290
Here's your container.

00:29:31.328 --> 00:29:32.693
Oh.

00:29:36.299 --> 00:29:37.857
After I'm done here,

00:29:37.901 --> 00:29:39.562
a bunch of us are going
to go down to the resort.

00:29:39.603 --> 00:29:40.900
Why don't you come along?

00:29:40.937 --> 00:29:43.337
Thanks, but I'm going
to turn in early.

00:29:43.373 --> 00:29:44.738
Maybe another time.

00:29:44.774 --> 00:29:45.832
Okay.

00:29:59.489 --> 00:30:01.320
Good evening, Ensign.

00:30:01.358 --> 00:30:02.848
Mr. Neelix.

00:30:02.893 --> 00:30:04.155
I thought I'd log a little time

00:30:04.194 --> 00:30:05.957
in the Jefferies tubes
if that's all right.

00:30:06.029 --> 00:30:07.826
I was unaware you
were officially

00:30:07.864 --> 00:30:09.491
on an engineering work detail.

00:30:09.533 --> 00:30:11.626
Oh, it's not official,
not at all.

00:30:11.668 --> 00:30:13.659
But Lieutenant Torres
has been good enough

00:30:13.703 --> 00:30:15.796
to allow me to poke
around here and there...

00:30:15.839 --> 00:30:16.965
as time permits, of course.

00:30:17.007 --> 00:30:18.634
She has mentioned
your desire to become

00:30:18.675 --> 00:30:20.666
familiar with Starfleet
engineering protocols.

00:30:20.710 --> 00:30:22.371
I see no reason
why you can't proceed.

00:30:22.412 --> 00:30:23.777
Thank you.

00:30:28.785 --> 00:30:30.912
Ensign Vorik.

00:30:30.954 --> 00:30:32.819
Yes, Mr. Neelix?

00:30:32.856 --> 00:30:34.949
You're quite young.

00:30:34.991 --> 00:30:36.458
Is it difficult for you

00:30:36.493 --> 00:30:39.656
being so far away
from everything that's familiar?

00:30:39.696 --> 00:30:41.994
Had I been given the choice,

00:30:42.098 --> 00:30:44.760
I might not have chosen
to explore the Delta Quadrant.

00:30:44.801 --> 00:30:46.769
However, since we are here,

00:30:46.803 --> 00:30:50.500
I must say the challenges
are intriguing.

00:30:50.540 --> 00:30:54.101
Voyager is
a wonderful place to be.

00:30:54.144 --> 00:30:56.442
The people here
are very fortunate.

00:30:56.479 --> 00:30:58.003
I would concur.

00:32:03.947 --> 00:32:05.175
Did you get it?

00:32:05.215 --> 00:32:06.182
Where is it?

00:32:06.216 --> 00:32:07.183
I have to talk to you.

00:32:07.217 --> 00:32:08.184
Give it to me.

00:32:08.218 --> 00:32:10.448
I didn't get the warp plasma.

00:32:10.487 --> 00:32:12.182
What?!

00:32:12.222 --> 00:32:13.780
I couldn't do it.

00:32:13.823 --> 00:32:15.313
I just couldn't.

00:32:15.358 --> 00:32:18.293
We have to tell the truth.

00:32:18.328 --> 00:32:20.592
It's the only way
to make things right.

00:32:23.400 --> 00:32:24.799
We're dead men, Neelix.

00:32:24.834 --> 00:32:27.166
No. I have a plan.

00:32:27.203 --> 00:32:29.330
You two, stay where you are!

00:32:31.274 --> 00:32:32.639
Don't panic.

00:32:32.676 --> 00:32:33.734
Stay calm.

00:32:36.346 --> 00:32:38.314
I said stay where you are!

00:32:38.348 --> 00:32:40.509
What is this?

00:32:40.550 --> 00:32:42.882
You two are under arrest.

00:32:42.919 --> 00:32:44.284
Arrest?

00:32:44.321 --> 00:32:45.379
What's the charge?

00:32:45.422 --> 00:32:49.722
Conspiring with known
drug traffickers... and murder.

00:32:49.759 --> 00:32:50.748
Let's go!

00:32:56.666 --> 00:32:59.260
This is the criminal
who was killed...

00:32:59.302 --> 00:33:01.930
and these are
the two men we arrested.

00:33:02.005 --> 00:33:05.634
You can't seriously
regard this as viable evidence.

00:33:05.675 --> 00:33:09.634
I realize it's circumstantial,
but it is compelling.

00:33:09.679 --> 00:33:11.340
It proves absolutely nothing.

00:33:11.381 --> 00:33:13.372
It proves your two men
had a conversation

00:33:13.416 --> 00:33:16.852
with a narcotics dealer
only hours before he was killed.

00:33:16.886 --> 00:33:19.150
As the Captain said,
that proves nothing.

00:33:19.189 --> 00:33:20.781
I'm holding them
for questioning.

00:33:20.824 --> 00:33:22.815
They are prime suspects.

00:33:25.962 --> 00:33:27.953
I want my security officer
present

00:33:28.031 --> 00:33:29.658
during all interrogations.

00:33:29.699 --> 00:33:32.668
I'll take that
into consideration.

00:33:33.670 --> 00:33:35.661
But make no mistake about this.

00:33:35.705 --> 00:33:37.536
Someone will serve 50 years

00:33:37.574 --> 00:33:40.771
of cryostatic suspension
for that murder.

00:33:40.810 --> 00:33:42.471
If I were to let
this go unpunished,

00:33:42.512 --> 00:33:45.675
there would be anarchy
on this station within days.

00:33:45.715 --> 00:33:47.706
You make no mistake about this.

00:33:47.751 --> 00:33:49.582
I won't allow members
of my crew to be condemned

00:33:49.619 --> 00:33:51.814
for a crime they did not commit.

00:34:14.544 --> 00:34:15.841
This has gone too far.

00:34:15.879 --> 00:34:17.346
We have to go to Bahrat.

00:34:17.380 --> 00:34:20.645
We'll end up in his
cryostatic prison for decades.

00:34:20.683 --> 00:34:22.583
Not if he agrees to my plan.

00:34:22.619 --> 00:34:24.678
Your plan is crazy.

00:34:24.721 --> 00:34:26.154
It's worse than prison.

00:34:26.189 --> 00:34:27.588
It's a death sentence.

00:34:27.624 --> 00:34:29.819
That would be better
than living a lie.

00:34:29.859 --> 00:34:31.884
I'm going whether you do or not.

00:34:31.928 --> 00:34:33.020
Neelix.

00:34:35.765 --> 00:34:38.063
We've been through
too much together.

00:34:38.101 --> 00:34:41.332
I can't let you do this alone.

00:34:49.813 --> 00:34:52.782
It was a type-2 Federation
phaser that was used.

00:34:52.816 --> 00:34:54.215
It's on one of our shuttles.

00:34:54.250 --> 00:34:56.514
You can get it
from our security officer

00:34:56.553 --> 00:34:58.384
to verify the energy signature.

00:34:58.421 --> 00:35:00.651
Which of you fired the weapon?

00:35:00.690 --> 00:35:03.284
We were both involved
in all aspects of the crime.

00:35:03.326 --> 00:35:05.157
I was the one with the weapon,

00:35:05.195 --> 00:35:07.720
but I fired in self-defense.

00:35:07.764 --> 00:35:09.732
So you see, Commander Chakotay

00:35:09.766 --> 00:35:12.064
and Lieutenant Paris
are innocent.

00:35:13.570 --> 00:35:16.937
The punishment for trafficking
in illicit substances

00:35:16.973 --> 00:35:20.340
is 50 years
of cryostatic imprisonment.

00:35:25.048 --> 00:35:28.506
Your cryostatic prison

00:35:28.551 --> 00:35:31.384
isn't a particularly
effective deterrent, is it?

00:35:31.421 --> 00:35:32.649
It certainly is.

00:35:32.689 --> 00:35:35.249
There's very little
narcotics trafficking

00:35:35.291 --> 00:35:36.492
that goes on here.

00:35:36.625 --> 00:35:38.786
That's what you think.

00:35:38.827 --> 00:35:42.024
The Kolaati have made a fortune
trading drugs here.

00:35:43.365 --> 00:35:46.334
I know everything
that happens on this station.

00:35:46.368 --> 00:35:47.835
Apparently not.

00:35:47.870 --> 00:35:50.168
Since we were able
to deliver narcotics

00:35:50.205 --> 00:35:52.969
to known criminals
right under your nose.

00:35:53.041 --> 00:35:56.568
They have ways of disabling
your surveillance systems.

00:35:56.612 --> 00:35:58.102
Masking your sensors.

00:35:58.146 --> 00:36:00.239
Creating false visual signals.

00:36:00.282 --> 00:36:02.375
It happens almost every night.

00:36:02.417 --> 00:36:04.885
I'll put a stop to that.

00:36:04.920 --> 00:36:06.820
Since you don't know
how they do it,

00:36:06.855 --> 00:36:08.550
that might prove difficult.

00:36:10.192 --> 00:36:12.558
But... we have a plan.

00:36:14.029 --> 00:36:17.931
The Kolaati want a sample
of warp plasma from Voyager.

00:36:18.033 --> 00:36:20.593
I'll arrange a meeting with them
to deliver the plasma.

00:36:20.636 --> 00:36:23.161
When they arrive,
we'll take them into custody.

00:36:23.205 --> 00:36:25.901
How do you plan to do that?

00:36:25.941 --> 00:36:28.603
You won't be able
to carry weapons

00:36:28.644 --> 00:36:31.374
and if they thought
my men and I were near,

00:36:31.413 --> 00:36:33.438
they'd be gone in a second.

00:36:33.482 --> 00:36:35.541
We have some ideas.

00:36:35.584 --> 00:36:38.883
If we are able
to turn them over to you,

00:36:38.921 --> 00:36:42.015
will you agree
not to charge us with a crime?

00:36:47.195 --> 00:36:49.186
It's no risk to me.

00:36:52.434 --> 00:36:56.962
You'll undoubtedly perish
in this ridiculous scheme.

00:36:57.005 --> 00:36:59.872
You'll have to provide us
with a sample of warp plasma.

00:36:59.908 --> 00:37:01.273
I won't take any from Voyager.

00:37:01.310 --> 00:37:03.744
What I can give you
won't be of the same quality.

00:37:03.779 --> 00:37:05.110
Doesn't matter.

00:37:05.147 --> 00:37:06.307
We'll make do.

00:37:07.349 --> 00:37:10.011
All right.
We'll try it.

00:37:10.052 --> 00:37:14.614
But I don't hold any hopes
that you will survive.

00:37:21.029 --> 00:37:22.087
It's been over 20 minutes.

00:37:22.130 --> 00:37:23.097
Where are they?

00:37:23.131 --> 00:37:24.860
I confirmed the time and place.

00:37:24.900 --> 00:37:26.060
They should be here.

00:37:26.101 --> 00:37:28.501
Maybe they've realized
it's a trap.

00:37:28.537 --> 00:37:29.834
Maybe they're not going
to show up.

00:37:29.871 --> 00:37:30.838
Let's hope they do

00:37:30.872 --> 00:37:32.965
or we will end up
in Bahrat's prison.

00:37:41.950 --> 00:37:43.247
It looks like

00:37:43.285 --> 00:37:46.721
somebody's begun transmitting
a false visual signal.

00:37:46.755 --> 00:37:50.521
My guess is they're
about to come aboard.

00:37:53.295 --> 00:37:55.320
We'll give them five minutes

00:37:55.364 --> 00:37:58.094
and then move in.

00:38:02.537 --> 00:38:03.697
It's Tosin.

00:38:03.739 --> 00:38:05.001
Who?

00:38:05.040 --> 00:38:07.270
He's one of the most
powerful Kolaati.

00:38:16.151 --> 00:38:17.277
Good evening, gentlemen.

00:38:17.319 --> 00:38:18.752
My name is Neelix, and I am...

00:38:18.787 --> 00:38:19.913
The warp plasma.

00:38:20.022 --> 00:38:21.046
Where is it?

00:38:21.089 --> 00:38:22.750
It's right in here, Tosin,

00:38:22.791 --> 00:38:25.055
but first, you must
guarantee us...

00:38:25.093 --> 00:38:26.082
You'll live for today.

00:38:26.128 --> 00:38:29.188
No guarantees about tomorrow.

00:38:29.231 --> 00:38:30.892
Give me the plasma.

00:38:30.932 --> 00:38:32.832
Slowly.

00:38:52.320 --> 00:38:56.347
20 parts per million
isonucleic residue.

00:38:56.391 --> 00:38:58.757
This is contaminated.

00:38:58.794 --> 00:39:01.058
You promised me a pure sample.

00:39:01.096 --> 00:39:02.563
It really doesn't matter,

00:39:02.597 --> 00:39:04.428
because you're under arrest.

00:39:04.466 --> 00:39:05.558
What?

00:39:05.600 --> 00:39:08.797
I said
you're being taken into custody

00:39:08.837 --> 00:39:12.136
for smuggling contraband
and narcotic substances.

00:39:12.174 --> 00:39:16.167
Very serious offenses
aboard this station, Mr. Tosin.

00:39:16.211 --> 00:39:18.179
It's time you faced up to them.

00:39:25.120 --> 00:39:27.281
Little man...

00:39:27.322 --> 00:39:29.790
your days have ended.

00:39:29.825 --> 00:39:31.520
I wouldn't fire that weapon
if I were you.

00:39:31.560 --> 00:39:33.653
That plasma canister
you're holding...

00:39:33.695 --> 00:39:37.290
I disengaged the safety nodes
just as you came in.

00:39:37.332 --> 00:39:40.631
Even as we speak,
warp plasma is leaking from it.

00:39:40.669 --> 00:39:43.797
This section
of the station is filling

00:39:43.839 --> 00:39:45.636
with plasma particles.

00:39:45.674 --> 00:39:47.039
Fire your weapon

00:39:47.075 --> 00:39:49.100
and you'll set off an explosion

00:39:49.144 --> 00:39:51.408
that would undoubtedly
kill us all.

00:39:51.446 --> 00:39:52.936
He's telling the truth, Tosin.

00:39:53.048 --> 00:39:54.208
Don't do it.

00:39:54.249 --> 00:39:55.614
And I wouldn't

00:39:55.650 --> 00:39:58.949
activate your transporter
system, if I were you.

00:39:59.054 --> 00:40:01.750
The beam would also
destabilize the plasma.

00:40:01.790 --> 00:40:03.280
Same effect.

00:40:03.325 --> 00:40:04.383
Boom.

00:40:06.962 --> 00:40:10.159
Then you will die with me,
little man.

00:40:10.198 --> 00:40:11.631
No problem at all

00:40:11.666 --> 00:40:12.963
if it means getting rid

00:40:13.068 --> 00:40:15.229
of an Orillian lung maggot
like you.

00:40:16.705 --> 00:40:17.865
Go ahead.

00:40:17.906 --> 00:40:20.898
You'd be doing me a favor.

00:40:20.942 --> 00:40:22.933
I have nothing to lose.

00:40:22.978 --> 00:40:24.138
Fire away.

00:40:24.179 --> 00:40:25.771
Neelix.

00:40:25.814 --> 00:40:26.906
Shoot.

00:40:26.948 --> 00:40:28.347
What are you waiting for?

00:40:30.185 --> 00:40:31.311
Fire.

00:40:45.567 --> 00:40:47.933
Re-engage the safety nodes.

00:40:47.969 --> 00:40:49.766
Don't bother.

00:40:49.805 --> 00:40:51.170
Put down your weapons.

00:40:51.206 --> 00:40:55.609
You're under arrest
for violating Station Code 4279,

00:40:55.644 --> 00:40:58.340
Subsection Beta-325.

00:40:59.915 --> 00:41:01.075
No, don't!

00:41:15.597 --> 00:41:17.565
I'm in Sick Bay?

00:41:17.599 --> 00:41:19.430
Yes, Mr. Neelix.

00:41:19.467 --> 00:41:21.059
You sustained
third-degree plasma burns

00:41:21.102 --> 00:41:22.194
and a moderate concussion,

00:41:22.237 --> 00:41:23.898
but my skills
have prevented you

00:41:23.939 --> 00:41:25.668
from suffering permanent damage.

00:41:25.707 --> 00:41:27.766
Thank you, Doctor.

00:41:27.809 --> 00:41:30.369
One of the criminals was killed
in the plasma explosion.

00:41:30.412 --> 00:41:32.846
The others have been taken
into custody by Mr. Bahrat.

00:41:32.881 --> 00:41:34.712
Chakotay and Tom were released.

00:41:34.749 --> 00:41:37.582
Oh, good.

00:41:37.619 --> 00:41:38.881
And Wix?

00:41:38.920 --> 00:41:40.979
Mr. Wixiban
was given his shuttle.

00:41:41.056 --> 00:41:43.957
He sent you his thanks
before making a hasty departure.

00:41:45.794 --> 00:41:47.318
Would all of you excuse us
please?

00:41:47.362 --> 00:41:48.920
I'd like to talk
to Neelix alone.

00:41:59.774 --> 00:42:02.709
Well, do you have
anything to say for yourself?

00:42:02.744 --> 00:42:05.872
Only that I'm terribly sorry.

00:42:05.914 --> 00:42:06.881
Oh.

00:42:06.915 --> 00:42:08.940
You're sorry.

00:42:09.050 --> 00:42:11.109
Is that supposed
to make everything better?

00:42:11.152 --> 00:42:14.053
I don't really care whether
you're sorry or not, Neelix.

00:42:14.089 --> 00:42:16.080
At this point it doesn't matter.

00:42:16.124 --> 00:42:19.116
I can't imagine what could have
made you behave the way you did.

00:42:19.160 --> 00:42:20.957
Lying to us.

00:42:21.062 --> 00:42:23.155
Sneaking around
behind our backs.

00:42:23.198 --> 00:42:25.598
Covering up criminal activity.

00:42:25.634 --> 00:42:27.329
Did you have
some misguided reason

00:42:27.369 --> 00:42:29.599
to think that this was
acceptable behavior?

00:42:29.638 --> 00:42:31.435
No, ma'am.

00:42:33.541 --> 00:42:36.066
You've been one
of my most trusted advisors

00:42:36.111 --> 00:42:37.806
since we began this journey.

00:42:37.846 --> 00:42:41.407
How can I ever trust you again?

00:42:41.449 --> 00:42:43.384
How can I ever listen to you

00:42:43.517 --> 00:42:46.247
without wondering whether you're
telling the truth or not?

00:42:48.989 --> 00:42:50.718
I've never been
dishonest to you before.

00:42:50.758 --> 00:42:52.658
I swear, Captain.

00:42:52.693 --> 00:42:56.754
I-I just took one step,

00:42:56.797 --> 00:43:00.255
a step that seemed
perfectly reasonable,

00:43:00.300 --> 00:43:02.495
and that step led
to another and another

00:43:02.536 --> 00:43:03.696
and before I knew it,

00:43:03.737 --> 00:43:06.069
I was involved in something
I didn't know how to handle.

00:43:06.106 --> 00:43:07.664
What was it?

00:43:07.708 --> 00:43:09.471
What was so important

00:43:09.510 --> 00:43:12.104
that you were willing
to throw away your principles?

00:43:13.614 --> 00:43:15.445
I needed a map.

00:43:15.482 --> 00:43:17.473
A map?

00:43:19.787 --> 00:43:22.813
Captain, my usefulness
to you was at an end.

00:43:22.856 --> 00:43:25.950
I don't know anything about
space beyond this point.

00:43:26.026 --> 00:43:29.086
I couldn't let you go
into the Nekrit Expanse

00:43:29.129 --> 00:43:31.029
without knowing what you faced.

00:43:33.066 --> 00:43:35.364
You've been on this ship
for two years.

00:43:35.402 --> 00:43:36.835
I'd think by now
you'd have learned

00:43:36.870 --> 00:43:38.701
that the first duty
of any Starfleet officer

00:43:38.739 --> 00:43:40.730
is the truth.

00:43:40.774 --> 00:43:43.299
You violated that duty, Neelix,

00:43:43.343 --> 00:43:46.540
and there will be consequences.

00:43:54.054 --> 00:43:55.988
I'm prepared to leave
the ship, Captain.

00:43:56.056 --> 00:43:58.923
Oh, no.
It's not that easy.

00:43:58.959 --> 00:44:01.757
You can't just walk away
from your responsibilities

00:44:01.795 --> 00:44:03.319
because you made a mistake.

00:44:03.363 --> 00:44:07.163
You're part of a family now,
and you have obligations.

00:44:08.535 --> 00:44:10.196
But...

00:44:10.237 --> 00:44:11.204
I can't guide you.

00:44:11.238 --> 00:44:12.205
I can't advise you.

00:44:12.239 --> 00:44:13.638
I don't know what's coming.

00:44:13.674 --> 00:44:15.665
That's not the point.

00:44:15.709 --> 00:44:17.040
Is it?

00:44:17.077 --> 00:44:19.068
None of us knows what's coming.

00:44:19.112 --> 00:44:21.706
That's what Starfleet
is all about.

00:44:21.748 --> 00:44:23.545
We are all in this together,
Neelix,

00:44:23.584 --> 00:44:25.950
and we have to be able
to count on each other

00:44:26.019 --> 00:44:27.509
no matter how hard it gets.

00:44:27.554 --> 00:44:30.045
Do you understand?

00:44:30.090 --> 00:44:31.717
Yes.

00:44:31.758 --> 00:44:33.419
Yes, I do.

00:44:33.460 --> 00:44:35.087
Well, that's good.

00:44:35.128 --> 00:44:39.189
Report to deuterium maintenance
at 0400 tomorrow morning.

00:44:39.233 --> 00:44:41.360
You're going to spend
the next two weeks

00:44:41.401 --> 00:44:43.164
scrubbing the exhaust manifolds.

00:44:43.203 --> 00:44:46.195
That should give you time
to think about what I've said.

00:44:46.240 --> 00:44:47.867
Dismissed.
